                    briefing_text_r3:       `Credible intervention demand exceeds the budget. Allocate the full <strong>€4.2M</strong> under the hard ceiling — and make the politically hard move: <em>reduce</em> the early-career third's <strong>78%</strong> share to fund mid-career and senior sustainability. But rebalancing is a <strong>redesign</strong>, not a zero-sum raid: if you cut early-career spend, offer that group something else (stretch roles, mentoring, guardrails) or you'll trigger high-potential flight. Name the one under-funded intervention that poses the largest grievance risk — the works council is watching the neglected groups.`,
